    T43
        title       Production code uses Effect's features instead of hand-rolled ones (audit R1 to R8)
        status      done
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T16]
        description
            `src/` applies the user-confirmed Effect simplification recommendations R1 to R8.

            **Why now:** the audit found hand-rolled clock, scheduler and fiber bookkeeping in the host, codecs
            built per call, and a real bug (event payloads never decoded); T17 onward would build on them.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/effect-simplification-2026-11-11.md;
            AGENTS.md "Code style (v3 production)"; @spec.Turn, @spec.Actors.

            **Approach:** R2's payload decoding first, then R1 (Host to Effect services, one FiberMap in the
            Runtime's Scope; dispose shuts the core down before closing the Scope), R3, R4, R5 to R8. Each lands
            alone with the suite green on round-14 and the Pay cases green on production.

            - **May change:** `packages/flow-state-v3/src/`, the production adapter, lint configuration.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a refactor that changes behaviour unnoticed → caught by the suite on production and
              the production mutants.
            - **Stops:** a guarantee change.
        acceptance
