    T44
        title       The suite judges from its own facts only, gated by machines
        status      done
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T43]
        description
            No path leads from a runtime report to an obligation, enforced by type and lint, and machine gates run
            on every checkpoint.

            **Why now:** six reviews found the same class, a report deciding an obligation; the advisor's Q1, Q6,
            Q7 and Q9 replace instance fixes with a structural rule and gates.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/advisor-answers-2026-11-11.md (Q0, Q1, Q6, Q7, 
            Q9); conformance/dsl/oracle.ts.

            **Approach:** split `Fact` so obligation code cannot see a report, with a lint ban; a liar gate (a
            mutant's acts with a correct runtime's recorded reports must stay red); a diffed catch matrix; generic
            mutants of `src/core` (a two-hour StrykerJS trial, else a small operator mutator); a crash generator; a
            generated gate file that notes and reports cite instead of hand-copied numbers.

            - **May change:** `packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/`, lint configuration, `package.json` scripts.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments; the generated gate file.
            - **False pass:** a report path left open → caught by the liar gate.
        acceptance
            - obligation code takes no runtime report (type and lint enforced);
            - under the liar gate no behavioural mutant turns green;
            - catch matrix, core mutants, crash generator and gate file run on every checkpoint.

    T45
        title       An executable Spec model computes expected results and generates cases (pilot: persistence)
        status      done
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T44]
        description
            One executable model written from the Specs computes each case's expected result and generates runs,
            piloted on the persistence area, replacing hand-written cases there.

            **Why now:** 111 Invariants are still owed; the advisor's Q2, Q3 and Q5 find generated runs from one
            model cheaper and stronger than hand cases, with round-14 kept as a mutant host.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/advisor-answers-2026-11-11.md (Q2, Q3, Q5); 
            @spec.WriteAhead; conformance/dsl/case.ts; @spec.Conformance.R19 to R22
            (the model's limits, the generic compare, facts only, the limits list; tests T32, T37, T38, T40 to T43 are
            this Task's).

            **Approach:** the model is the existing `dsl/lifecycle*.ts` modules (rules, step, owed), adapted, and
            imports nothing from a runtime; generated runs are a reload after every step of
            the existing cases, the old suite's search, and seeded sequences with shrinking; hand cases become the
            model's tests; round-14 becomes a mutant host with a limits list a run verifies.

            **Owns (records review, 2026-11-11):** the script Schema, the script player and the shrinker, over hand
            fixtures; @task.V3.T47 reuses them for parts and builds none of its own (@spec.Conformance.R15, R22). The
            generators run on round-14, still with no composite.

            **Narrowed (replan, accepted 2026-11-11), slice R:** first restore the disposal catch of
            `o6.settled-in-bound-stays-held`, so falsify round-14 is 147/147 and nothing else in the Epic starts red.
            Then the expect/compare split (obligation code takes no observation; lint covers `lifecycle-step.ts`,
            `lifecycle-owed.ts` and `turn/selection.ts`; claim cells collapse into a generic compare), the model's
            rollback to the last landed capture at a kill, and three generators (a crash at every step, the small
            exhaustive search, and seeded `fc.commands` runs with shrinking to regression files). Adds `limits.ts` with
            its gate. Absorbs @task.V3.T14 (searches and mutants as runner modes; the machine verdict form). Effort 3
            (estimate). Read code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/replan-2026-11-11.md (part 3, "R Rework").

            **Remaining steps, in order** (rebuilt 2026-11-11; the lead's scratchpad plan is gone):

            1. Restore the disposal catch of `o6.settled-in-bound-stays-held` (falsify round-14 147/147). Keep a parked
               ending saved in disposal owed; allow only unsaved definite endings.
            2. Evidence endings (Released, Superseded) and parked endings saved by no landing, in the lifecycle and in
               evidence-kinds (PAY-03@7, DISP-0x); the PAY-07 and DLV-06 leaves.
            3. Expect/compare split: report-free owed members; lint on `lifecycle-step.ts`, `lifecycle-owed.ts` and
               `turn/selection.ts`; claim cells into one generic compare (Conformance R19, R20, T38, T40).
            4. The model's rollback to the last landed capture at a kill (production crash 70 red; Restore R3,
               WriteAhead R10); rerun `crash --runtime production` (the Held-head bug stays for @task.V3.T51).
            5. Script Schema, player and shrinker; the generators (crash at every step, small exhaustive search, seeded
               `fc.commands` runs) with regressions kept (T32); round-14 kill counts (acceptance 1).
            6. `limits.ts` with its gate (T42), the liar greens on round-14 (T41), the runner's default runtime
               production (T43), model purity lint (T37), the runner modes of @task.V3.T14.

            **Phase-out, steps 0 to 2 (the user accepted 2026-11-11,
            code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/conformance-phase-out-2026-11-11.md):**

            - Step 0, with step 1 above: refresh `gates.json` at HEAD and add `falsify --sweep` records per runtime
              (`catch-sweep.<runtime>.tsv`, mutant by case) and the coverage standings per Invariant; every later
              phase-out step compares against them.
            - Step 1, with step 3: delete `lifecycle-perturbations.ts` and the `claimed` handling in
              `lifecycle-owed.ts`; Table A's refusing cells stay as the compare's named refusals (amended, the user,
              2026-11-12); liar round-14 greens no more than 9.
            - Step 2, with step 6: `limits.ts` rows replace the round-14 reasons in `not-yet.ts` and the README.
            - **Gap:** five scenario files hold checks only case expectations make (schedules, lane-keys,
              payment-retry, parts, refusal; `suite.ts` `caseChecks`); they wait for an oracle or the model, here or
              in @task.V3.T52.

            - **May change:** `packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/`.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** the model shares a runtime's misreading → caught by a different model family reading
              a sample of expectations, and by the mutants.
        acceptance
            - on round-14 with the suite's mutants, generated runs alone kill at least as many as the hand cases in
              the area;
            - the search finds at least one Spec conflict or runtime difference no case had, or reports none;
            - falsify round-14 is 147/147 before any other step of this Task.
            - the persistence rows of @task.V3.T10 (now the suite half of @task.V3.T19) are covered by generated runs.
            - obligation code takes no observation, enforced by lint on every expect module: `dsl/expect.ts`,
              `turn/predict.ts` and what they import (`dsl/lifecycle*.ts`, `turn/anchor.ts`, the fixtures' folds).
            - `limits.ts` rows each fail on round-14 by their named Invariant, and a gate verifies it.
            - searches and mutants run from the one runner with `--parallel`, a planted slow child reads as unknown, and
              the old suite's search kills in this suite's areas are reproduced, those of Reads and Sessions owned
              by @task.V3.T21 and @task.V3.T25 (from @task.V3.T14; amended, the user, 2026-11-12).
            - Phase-out steps 0 to 2 are done: the baseline sweeps and `gates.json` at HEAD exist, the perturbations and
              claim cells are gone, and `limits.ts` replaces the prose reasons.
            - Phase-out checks (the four validations): no lost catch in the catch matrix; the same coverage and
              feature-matrix rows; the derived reference equal to the hand rows wherever both exist;
              Compile static cases green on each fixture's `Compiled`.
    T47
        title       Fixture infrastructure and pilot parts: shapes, scripts, capability lists, gates (slice R)
        status      done
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T51]
        description
            Build the fixture infrastructure and pilot it on three composite parts: `shape()` modules as data, scripts
            as JSON, a script player, runtime capability lists, the reach recorder, the feature matrix with the
            combination gate, and the `bench` runner (slice R).

            **Why now:** about 70 of 112 hand cases use one application (checkout Pay); the user wants a wide net of
            flows, state transitions and network faults, written once and read by the generator, the Spec model and the
            benchmark replay (2026-11-11). Composites run on production and the model only; round-14 stays a mutant host
            for the 99 hand cases, which freeze.

            **Read first:** @task.V3.T45, code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/fixture-catalogue-2026-11-11.md
            (sections 2, 4, 5A, 5B and 7), code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/replan-2026-11-11.md (part 3,
            "R Rework"), conformance/world/network.ts,
            @spec.Conformance.R15 to R23 (tests T30, T31, T33 to T36, T39, T44 are this Task's),
            code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/plan-task-coverage-2026-11-11.md (the 265 features).

            **Builds on T45:** the script Schema, player and shrinker are @task.V3.T45's; this Task adds parts and the
            scripts generated from them, and writes no second set.

            **Risk:** the interacting-pair count is an estimate (671 by the replan's reading, 777 by the catalogue's).
            The reach recorder measures it, and the user approves the non-interacting rules once, as one list (replan
            question 12).

            **Approach, progressive fixtures:** fixtures grow with the slices, so no part waits on a missing runtime
            feature. Each part declares the feature codes it needs. Each runtime (production, the Spec model, round-14)
            declares the codes it implements. The generator enables only operations whose codes the runtime has. The
            feature-matrix gate reads a feature with no runtime as "owed by slice N" and fails one that a runtime
            implements but no fixture covers. The combination gate counts only pairs among implemented codes. A part
            lands in the slice that builds its first feature and gains operations as later slices land theirs.

            **Approach, build:** one `shape()` module per part, with its reference derived from production's `Compiled`,
            a user model and a server model; usual and stress profiles; the app mix; the matrix maps all 265 Plan
            features, each row naming its fixture kind (composite part, hand case, static case, example-app check or 
            package
            check). Pilot parts: S16 into C, S21 flattened into H, S10 into I (39 interacting pairs, an estimate).
            Composites A to K are placed by slice in the replan's part tables; J and K (catalogue 5B) are built in slice
            3 with the subset available. S27 and the Plan-check shapes arrive with their slices. Effort 4 (estimate).

            **Catalogue correction:** the catalogue's section 1 claims (production writes under four policies and has
            `cancelAll`) and its P tiers (section 7: 11 shapes run on production now) are wrong for production today
            (replan part 1). The catalogue file is not edited; this Task's matrix and the slice tables supersede them.

            **Declares today's codes:** the 15 codes production implements now (the replan's R row), listed from
            `adapters/production.ts` and recorded in this Task's comments.

            **Bench:** turn cost per part (median and p99) is recorded as a measurement, not a gate; only the work
            fingerprint check gates (the user declined up-front optimisation, 2026-11-11).

            **Order:** one lead at a time: T45, then T51, then T47; in every slice the suite half finishes before the
            production half, by the same builder or the next.

            **Phase-out, step 3 (the user accepted 2026-11-11,
            code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/conformance-phase-out-2026-11-11.md):** this Task builds
            `referenceOf(compiled)` (events, states, handlers, schedules, rows, each operation's concurrency, key fields
            and ending map); the hand descriptors still exist, so it retires nothing and records the V4 baseline. It
            also builds the production static surface (`construct` and the data view), moved from @task.V3.T17, so the
            Compile static cases run on production's `Compiled` (`runner/args.ts:46-51` binds the null surface today).

            **Layout (accepted):** `packages/flow-state-v3/fixtures/` holds real machines and imports only
            `src/index.ts`; `packages/flow-state-v3/bench/` sits beside it and imports the world and player from
            `conformance/`; `conformance/` is the input/output validator and a lint stops it importing `bench/`.
            Expected results come only from the Spec model or a written ruling, and every bug found becomes a shrunk
            regression script. The model search replaces the hand traces, apart from those that record a ruling.

            **Gap (blocking):** production has no static surface yet; built here.

            **Gap (blocking):** `classify` (a commit's answer to a channel) is not in `Compiled`, so each fixture
            declares it beside its server model.

            - **May change:** `packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/`, `packages/flow-state-v3/fixtures/`,
              `packages/flow-state-v3/bench/` (fixtures, world, generator, runner).
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments; the generated gate file.
            - **False pass:** parts that differ in name but reach the same cells → caught by table-cell reach and model
              mutation across parts.
            - **Gates:** matrix, combination, falsify, liar and core-mutant gates; `nub run check`.
            - **Stops:** the user's approval of the non-interacting pair list.
        acceptance
            - the combination gate: every unreached interacting pair has a dated owner (Conformance R18);
            - `shape()` modules, JSON scripts and the script player exist: a script generated from a part replays under
              the oracles on production, and the Spec model computes its expected reports.
            - each fixture part declares the feature codes it needs, and each runtime (production, the Spec model,
              round-14) declares the codes it implements.
            - the generator enables only operations whose codes the runtime has.
            - the feature-matrix gate treats a feature with no runtime as "owed by slice N", fails a feature a runtime
              implements that is in no fixture, and maps all 265 Plan features with the fixture kind per row.
            - the combination gate counts only pairs among implemented codes, takes the interacting-pair list from the
              channel table, fails an unexercised pair with no dated waiver, and reports triples and cell-pair reach.
            - the pilot parts S16 [C], S21 flattened [H] and S10 [I] each have usual and stress profiles, kill
              table-cell mutants of the model, and run on production, alone and in the app mix.
            - the `bench` runner replays the same scripts without oracles and reproduces the work fingerprint; turn cost
              per part is recorded (median and p99) as a measurement, not a gate; the fingerprint check is a gate.
            - every failure found shrinks to a kept regression case or is logged as a runtime limit.
            - Declared: the capability lists exist and today's implemented codes are declared in each.
            - Enabled: S16, S21 and S10 declare their needs and the generator draws only declared operations.
            - Covered: the combination gate passes over the pairs among today's implemented codes.
            - Guards: production's first-contact reds are recorded and classified, held-out seeds pass, and a sample of
              the model's expectations is read by a different model family (Fable).
            - the non-interacting pair list is generated from the channel table, and the user approves its rules once,
              as one list.
            - the Compile static cases run on every composite's `Compiled`.
            - Phase-out step 3: `referenceOf(compiled)` exists; the production static surface (`construct`, data view)
              exists; each fixture declares `classify` beside its server model; `fixtures/` imports only
              `src/index.ts`, `bench/` sits beside it, and a lint bars `conformance/` from importing `bench/`.
            - Phase-out checks (the four validations): no lost catch in the catch matrix; the same coverage and
              feature-matrix rows; the derived reference equal to the hand rows wherever both exist; Compile static
              cases green on each fixture's `Compiled`.
    T52
        title       Suite phase-out, first cut: Pay and Cells generated, hand traces thinned
        status      done
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T60]
        description
            Pay and Cells become generated parts in the top-level `fixtures/`; Pay's hand rows stay as one frozen
            golden; the hand traces give way to the model search (phase-out step 4).

            **Why now:** the user accepted the phase-out (2026-11-11), including Pay as a generated part, which reverses
            replan decision 5 ("Pay is not converted") for Pay. Without this cut the suite keeps two descriptions of
            Pay and two judges of every run.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/conformance-phase-out-2026-11-11.md (step 4,
            validations V1 to V4), @task.V3.T47, @task.V3.T45, @spec.Conformance.R15.

