    T60
        title       The suite proves its own gates and excuses
        status      done
        priority    high
        description
            The suite's excuse lists are proven: every excuse names its exact subject and must still fail, a planted
            fault anywhere else in any owed script fails a gate, and one rule says what "caught" means.

            **Why now:** 128 holes found by reviews in T47 and T52 trace to one gap: the suite proves its oracles but
            never its own gates or excuse lists, and only one hole was ever found by a machine. The user, 2026-11-14:
            pause T52 and do this first, since T52's remaining steps (the one owed list, trace thinning) build on it.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/suite-convergence-2026-11-14.md (the design
            of record, its recommendation and its "missing rules"), @spec.Conformance,
            conformance/parts/owed.ts.

            **Approach:** the reduced design (the user, 2026-11-14), built at once:
            - excuses by exact subject (Attempt, or step and fact), never text, kind or count;
            - every listed item still fails, and an item whose owner Task is done fails;
            - a planted-fault sweep over every owed script and seed as the class gate, run at every checkpoint;
            - the parts gate plays every owed script at every seed;
            - structured verdicts and one "caught" rule replacing the five.
            The paused T52 redesign items are this Task's first step. Cut to revisit.md until holes show they are
            needed: mutation of the suite's own code, per-gate universe ledgers, one excuse registry, the unknowns
            ledger.

            False pass: an excuse that matches more than it names → caught by the planted-fault sweep.
            Gates: falsify, the class gate, `nub run check`.
        acceptance
            - a planted lost ending on any fresh subject, in any owed script at any seed, fails a gate;
            - an excuse whose item stops failing, or whose owner Task is done, fails a gate;
            - one function decides "caught" from structured verdicts, and the liar gate and probes use it;
            - falsify, liar and catch matrices keep their counts or each change is explained.
    T59
        title           The suite reads and imports nothing outside the package
        status          tombstone
        priority        high
        blocked_by      [@T47]
        description
            The conformance suite and the runner read no file, CLI or folder outside `packages/flow-state-v3/` and
            import nothing from `src/` beyond the seam; the data they read from the wiki today is recreated in the
            package as typed code.

            **Held:** runs only when the user says so, or once the project is built out (the user, 2026-11-14); it is
            in no slice order.

            **Why now:** the user, 2026-11-14: the package is self-contained (AGENTS.md, Code style). The suite's
            gates parse dated proposals by matching their prose, so a reworded proposal silently feeds them wrong text.
            Blocked by @T47, whose open files hold most of these reads.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/self-contained-audit-2026-11-14.md
            (groups A, E, F), conformance/parts/records.ts,
            conformance/runner/specs.ts.

            **Approach:** the feature rows, pair rules, slices and Spec Invariant lists become typed modules in the
            package. The check that a Task owner is still open is a fact about the wiki: it moves to
            `tools/plan-coverage`, beside `check:plans` (orchestrator, 2026-11-14). The gates file takes its revision
            from a runner argument, or records it as missing, visibly. Mutant copies resolve dependencies through the
            package's own declared ones. Concepts and comment citations (audit groups B, C, D, G) are not in scope:
            they are deferred to revisit.md (the user, 2026-11-14); round-14's prototype adapters stay as they are.

            False pass: a recreated table that drifts from the wiki → caught by the `tools/` check comparing them.
            Gates: every suite gate as before, green at the same counts; a planted outside read (a `wiki/` path, a
            `wk` call, `../../..` past the root) fails the new check.
            User's read: where each moved check now lives.
        acceptance
            - no `node:fs` read, child process or symlink in `conformance/` or `bench/` reaches outside the package,
              shown by a test that walks the source and plants one of each;
            - `conformance/` imports from `src/` only `src/index.ts` and the listed seam (audit group E);
            - `packages/flow-state-v3/package.json` declares the dependencies the package imports (audit group F);
            - every gate in `conformance/gates.json` keeps its verdict and counts at the Task's first and last
              revisions;
            - the wiki-facing checks (open owners, recreated tables against their source) run from `tools/` and fail
              on a planted mismatch.
        deletion_reason
            Superseded (the user, 2026-11-15): the conformance suite was deleted; its last copy is commit 52a883e6. The 
            rule now covers tests/ and is checked by grep at each review 
            (code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md, task A5).
    T61
        title       The suite runs itself and draws varied inputs
        status      done
        priority    high
        description
            The conformance gates run automatically, the generator varies its inputs, outputs the suite already computes
            become gates, failures shrink and group by root cause, a soak run finds new classes, and a trace command 
            shows
            each run's inputs and outcomes.

            **Why now:** the user, 2026-11-14, from 
            code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/suite-leverage-survey-2026-11-14.md
            (items 1 to 4 and 7): `verify` runs no conformance gate, answers always reach the oldest request and timers
            fire on their deadline, and several computed results gate nothing. Its cheap, file-disjoint parts run beside
            @task.V3.T52; the rest follows T52.

            **Approach:**
            - parallel with T52: the gates in `verify` and at each checkpoint; crash's three reds named and owned; the
              six kept regressions saved as passes re-saved or dropped; a trace command (step, expected, observed,
              mismatch);
            - after T52: out-of-order answers, timing offsets around deadlines, payloads varied by seed, a usual mix and
              Pay in a mix; cell-pair reach and the production sweep's neighbouring rows gated; part scripts shrunk
              automatically and failures grouped by signature; seeds chosen by reach; a soak run at each Task's close.

            False pass: a varied input the model mispredicts → caught by the model's own expected results, never the
            runtime's.
        acceptance
            - `nub run verify` runs the cheap conformance gates and fails on a red one;
            - a kept regression saved as a pass is re-saved from a real red or deleted;
            - every crash red is named in the gate output with an owner;
            - a trace file shows each step's input, the model's expected outcome, the observed outcome and any mismatch;
            - the generator draws out-of-order answers and timing offsets, and some run reaches a cell no run reached
              before;
            - a soak run shrinks each new failure and keeps one case per signature.
    T54
