        status      open
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T61, @task.V3.T67]
        description
            Consolidate production's core in steps A0 to A4: one ledger of owed endings, one `start`, records written
            from what each step touched, and every report built by `evidenceOf` from acts. Added (the user, 2026-11-14):
            production's own self-proof, meaning production mutants for the liar behaviours and the 29 owed core gaps,
            and coverage counting production's mutants (suite-leverage-survey-2026-11-14.md, item 5).

            **Why now:** an ending is held in four places (`World.parked`, `World.kept`, the lane's Kept state,
            `Tries`), and moves issue their own writes and reports through `persist`, `park`, `keep` and `tx.emit`;
            known bugs come from that (a second kept ending overwrites the first, @spec.Actors.I24; lane-less endings
            dropped at disposal). @task.V3.T18 builds four policies on this core, so it goes first. The user accepted
            this Task and its place on 2026-11-12 (Q1 A).

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/fable-architecture-consult-3-2026-11-12.md
            (the design of record: Part 2, C2 for steps, C3 for checks), @task.V3.T51, @spec.WriteLanes, @spec.Actors.
            Prior art: rounds 1 and 2,
            code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/fable-architecture-consult-2026-11-12.md and
            code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/fable-architecture-consult-2-2026-11-12.md.
            Blocked by @T52, which settles the suite this Task baselines against.

            **Brief** (proposed; source
            code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/core-task-briefs-2026-11-12.md): the sections below
            and the comments "Rules for every brief" and "Requirements (from core-task-briefs-2026-11-12.md)"
            are this Task's brief. The older comments are known gaps. Where this brief and the record disagree,
            the brief is newer.

            **Read first (added):** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/fable-architecture-consult-3-2026-11-12.md
            (Part 2, C2, C3, C9); `packages/flow-state-v3/prototypes/t54-skeleton` (the target types; it
            compiles); @spec.WriteLanes (R5, R6, R10, `algorithm`, I27 to I37); @spec.Actors (R8, R10, R15, R20 to
            R22, I40, I41); @spec.WriteAhead (R4, R5, R10, I20 to I22); @spec.Restore (R1, R3); @spec.Turn.R26;
            @spec.Codec.R5.

            **Record differences:**

            - The comment of 2026-11-12T07:14:01Z (GEN-pay-search-25) is stale: `974ad3a1` fixed the model and
              emptied `regressionsOwed`. No work is owed for it.
            - The record's cost baseline names S08 and S16; S08 does not exist until T18, so T54 measures on S16
              and T18 repeats the measure on S08.
            - The record's "five pending cases" are not in the suite yet: step A0 writes them (A-1 to A-5). They
              are owed, not present.

            **Decisions already made:**

            - Endings apply at settlement (`Cue.Answered`). The fallback (keep `Settled` as a fourth `Delivery`
              state) is allowed by wiki/specs/spec-log.md, not by a Spec, but the builder asks the orchestrator before
              taking it.
            - Only Kept rows block a key (`keptOn`). `Identity` is T9's. The capture window stays in the host.
            - Attempt ids: a seed of at least 128 bits per boot, never restored, plus the Attempts' own counter.
              The id's text form is the builder's, with one rule: two boots never give equal ids.
            - No new report kind: a row's birth is Ended, waiting is Parked, resuming is Unparked, closing is
              Delivered or Recorded. No `Owed` report, no `owed()` on the Port.
            - Records: three kinds, one `format` number, the field lists of @spec.WriteAhead.R5; one owed list per
              identity.
            - A saved row holds no `owner`, `current`, audience or delivery beyond `kept`: a row decoded from a
              record is owed to the identity, is Waiting (Kept when `kept`), and is delivered current from the
              active leaf (@spec.Turn.R20's adopted ending).
            - `start` owes no derived unknown { Restored } for a Held head on a Releasing lane (WriteLanes I15);
              it still moves every Waiting and Kept row. It walks lanes in lane-id order.
            - Promotion never waits on a Kept row. A Refused ending's turn leaves its row to the retry; Unhandled
              and Denied close it Delivered (@spec.Turn.R26).
            - Opaque types as in the skeleton: branded `Ledger` and `Life`; `Report` is the branded Evidence only
              `evidenceOf` returns. T54 keeps `World.life` in `Disposal`'s shape; `Life` is T55's.
            - T54 routes read endings through `owe` with their audience and changes nothing else about reads.

            **Parts:** the base parts, usual and stress; A-2 to A-4 and A-12 to A-15 need the stress profile's
            disposals, reloads and storage faults.

            **Requirements:** A-1 to A-19, in the comment "Requirements (from core-task-briefs-2026-11-12.md)";
            each is red first.

            **Steps** (each ends with all gates no worse, `nub run check` at zero, and a Task comment):

            - **A0, checks only, no core change.** Write A-1 to A-19's checks and wrong runtimes. Record the
              differential baseline: per step the reports, commands and store contents, over every production
              case and generated part, both seeds; the Task comment names where it lives. Add the cost scenarios
              to `bench/bench.ts` and record the cost baseline (turn cost; `ready()` with 64 queued declines; 500
              keyed lanes on S16). Also two guard checks: `unpark` is safe only because one step drains the mail;
              dropping the stored `mayHaveApplied` changes no report. **Check:** A-1 to A-6 red; A-11 green with
              its wrong runtime red; wrong runtimes for code that does not exist yet are listed as owed, each to
              the step that builds it.
            - **A1, the ledger in memory.** `World.owed` and the five functions replace `World.parked`,
              `World.kept` and `Tries`; `Cue.Answered` replaces `Settled` and `Ended`; `Keep`, the Kept lane
              state and `Settled.route` go; Attempts get their own counter and the 128-bit seed; old record keys
              are still written. **Check:** A-1, A-2, A-5 to A-11, A-18, A-19 green; baseline equal bar named
              entries.
            - **A2, one `start`.** Reload, return and adoption call it; `boot` parks nothing and
              `deliverRestored` goes. **Check:** A-3, A-12 green; post-boot reports equal per identity.
            - **A3, diff-written records.** Setters note touched lanes and identities; the step projects each
              changed entry once (`encodeActor`, `encodeLane`, `encodeOwed`); `Due` is derived (Awaited when a
              touched head entered Acknowledging or Recapturing, Now when an actor record is removed or an
              incarnation ended, else Later). `persist`, `park`, `keep` go. **Check:** A-4, A-13 to A-15 green;
              reload behaviour equal at every crash point (bytes may differ). Record the report stream for A-16.
            - **A4, acts into `evidenceOf`.** `tx.emit` and `insertEvidence` go; Evidence constructors are
              private to `evidence-of.ts`. **Check:** A-16, A-17 green; cost baseline re-run, both results in the
              Task comment.

            **Traps:**

            - **Mail holds a reference, not the ending.** A reference whose row is closed must do nothing, and a
              refusal adds a new reference behind queued mail. Copying the ending into mail brings the old bug
              back.
            - **Kept on its try is Retrying.** During a Start's one try the row does not block; if refused it is
              Kept again. A commit admitted in that window is allowed (WriteLanes R6).
            - **A1's adapter.** If keeping the old record keys needs an adapter larger than the step, the
              documented fallback is to merge A1 and A3; ask first.
            - **The byte-equal stream** in A4 is the refactor's strongest check. An "equal after sorting"
              comparison is a weaker check and needs the orchestrator.
            - **Old citations.** Conformance files cite reworded rules and a stored `mayHaveApplied`
              (`wiki/specs/spec-log.md`, last section). Update a citation when its file is touched; mutants
              that edit a stored `mayHaveApplied` are rewritten against `sentBefore`.

            **Must not decide alone:** taking the `Settled` fallback; merging A1 and A3; any allowed baseline
            difference that cites no pending case; `Identity`, the tagged result or one `Commit` cue (T9, T18);
            whether a row shows "kept" to user code (T18); any field of the three records beyond
            @spec.WriteAhead.R5's lists.

            **Handoffs** (comments on the receiving Task):

            - **T18:** a table over Idle and head phases; one `Answered` cue; `owe` and `keptOn`; no persist or
              emit API; Q5 as "close the lane's kept rows, then mint"; the cost baseline to repeat on S08.
            - **T19:** writes as a flat per-step list with `Due` derived; the batch-scope question; the
              Recapturing projection rule; the capture window still in the edge.
            - **T20:** three record kinds with `format`; a boot that sorts and derives Restored.
            - **T21:** read endings are rows with a chosen audience; `World.reads` untouched.
            - **T55:** `World.life` still `Disposal` in shape; the three places the host reads `driver.world()`
              (`src/host/runtime.ts:116, 132, 188`).

            **Decisions (orchestrator, 2026-11-12):**

            1. An ending is applied to its lane when its call settles (`Cue.Answered`), with a failing check first
               (a cancel between settlement and admission keeps the known success). Fallback, if backlog shows a
               real problem: keep `Settled` as a fourth `Delivery` state and the `Ended` cue.
            2. Only Kept rows block a key (`keptOn`).
            3. `Identity` is deferred to @task.V3.T9.
            4. The capture window stays in the host; moving it into the core is deferred.

            **Approach:** each step of round 3's C2 table, with its "must stay true" as the step's check.

            - A0: every C3 check written and red where it should be, baselines recorded, no core change; plus
              failing-first checks that `unpark` is safe only because one step drains, and that dropping the stored
              `mayHaveApplied` for `sentBefore` changes nothing.
            - A1: the ledger in memory, old record keys still written; `Settled` and `Ended` merge into `Answered`;
              `Keep`, the Kept row, `Tries` and `Settled.route` go; Attempts get their own counter.
            - A2: one `start` for reload, return and adoption; `boot` parks nothing.
            - A3: diff-written records and the three record kinds of C9.
            - A4: acts into `evidenceOf`; `tx.emit` and `insertEvidence` go; the report stream byte-equal to A3's.

            Each step ends with the suite, falsify, liar, crash and core-mutant gates no worse, `nub run check` at
            zero, and the differential baseline equal except for named entries. Handoffs follow round 3's "Task split
            and handoffs" table; the T18 to T21 items are comments on those Tasks.

            **Risk:** if A1 cannot keep the old record keys without an adapter larger than the step, merge A1 and A3
            and rely on the crash-point check alone (C2). Out of scope, owned elsewhere: `Life` (@task.V3.T55), the
            tagged result and one `Commit` cue (@task.V3.T18), read slots (@task.V3.T21), `owner`, `current` and the
            lateness field (@task.V3.T17), the record codec (@task.V3.T20).

            - **May change:** `packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/`, the host only where a removed API is called,
              `packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/` (pending cases, baselines, mutants), 
              `packages/flow-state-v3/bench/`.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments, which name where the baselines live.

            False pass: a refactor that changes behaviour unnoticed → caught by the differential baseline (each
            difference named and citing the pending case it flips) and reload equivalence at every crash point.
            Gates: suite, falsify, liar, crash and core mutants no worse than at A0; C3's design mutants, written
            before the code, each killed; `nub run check`.
            Stops: an allowed difference that cites no pending case (the refactor is changing behaviour); a guarantee
            change.
            User's read: the named allowed differences; whether the `Settled` fallback was taken.
        acceptance
            - A0 lands before any core change: C3's five pending cases red; the differential baseline (reports,
